# Shell environment bootstrap
#
# These have to exist before anything else in this repo works, and none of them
# were declared until a fresh-machine audit went looking. `make install-linux`
# runs linux.sh (which installs this list) and then calls `stow` directly, so
# without stow here the install died at that line with "command not found" —
# and linux.sh's `chsh -s "$ZSH_PATH"` step is guarded on zsh existing, so a
# missing zsh silently left the login shell as bash.
#
# git is listed for completeness even though cloning this repo already needed
# it. curl, wget, ca-certificates, gnupg2 and software-properties-common are
# deliberately absent: linux.sh installs them in its own prerequisite step,
# before this file is read, because adding the third-party repos depends on them.
stow
zsh
git

# xclip backs the `clip` helper in zsh/.local/bin. This machine runs KDE on X11;
# on Wayland `clip` prefers wl-copy, so add wl-clipboard if you switch.
xclip

# Test tooling — required by `make test`
# Note: actionlint has no apt package; install via: go install github.com/rhysd/actionlint/cmd/actionlint@latest
bats
shellcheck
expect

